+<DL>
+<DD><B>Deprecated.</B>&nbsp;<DD>Obtains a pool entry with a connection within the given timeout.
+ If <A HREF="../../../../../../org/apache/http/impl/conn/tsccm/PoolEntryRequest.html#abortRequest()"><CODE>abortRequest()</CODE></A> is called before this completes
+ an <A HREF="http://download.oracle.com/javase/1.5.0/docs/api/java/lang/InterruptedException.html" title="class or interface in java.lang"><CODE>InterruptedException</CODE></A> is thrown.
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>timeout</CODE> - the timeout, 0 or negative for no timeout<DD><CODE>tunit</CODE> - the unit for the <code>timeout</code>,
+                  may be <code>null</code> only if there is no timeout
+<DT><B>Returns:</B><DD>pool entry holding a connection for the route
+<DT><B>Throws:</B>
+<DD><CODE><A HREF="../../../../../../org/apache/http/conn/ConnectionPoolTimeoutException.html" title="class in org.apache.http.conn">ConnectionPoolTimeoutException</A></CODE> - if the timeout expired
