+<A NAME="domainMatch(java.lang.String, java.lang.String)"><!-- --></A><H3>
+domainMatch</H3>
+<PRE>
+public boolean <B>domainMatch</B>(<A HREF="http://download.oracle.com/javase/1.5.0/docs/api/java/lang/String.html" title="class or interface in java.lang">String</A>&nbsp;host,
+                           <A HREF="http://download.oracle.com/javase/1.5.0/docs/api/java/lang/String.html" title="class or interface in java.lang">String</A>&nbsp;domain)</PRE>
+<DL>
+<DD>Performs domain-match as defined by the RFC2965.
+ <p>
+ Host A's name domain-matches host B's if
+ <ol>
+   <ul>their host name strings string-compare equal; or</ul>
+   <ul>A is a HDN string and has the form NB, where N is a non-empty
+       name string, B has the form .B', and B' is a HDN string.  (So,
+       x.y.com domain-matches .Y.com but not Y.com.)</ul>
+ </ol>
+<P>
+<DD><DL>
+</DL>
+</DD>
+<DD><DL>
+<DT><B>Parameters:</B><DD><CODE>host</CODE> - host name where cookie is received from or being sent to.<DD><CODE>domain</CODE> - The cookie domain attribute.
+<DT><B>Returns:</B><DD>true if the specified host matches the given domain.</DL>
+</DD>
+</DL>
+<HR>
